        "original_id": "40703c7b-91cc-53f9-ad16-1c176a40db0c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kevin Rudd, Anthony Albanese, Chris Bowen, Quentin Bryce\n- Organizations: Australian government, Australian Labor Party, Australian House of Representatives\n- Roles: Prime Minister, Deputy Prime Minister, Treasurer, Governor-General, spokesperson on Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism\n- Places: Division of Grayndler\n- Events: Second Rudd Ministry\n\nFacts:\n- Anthony Albanese was born on 2 March 1963.\n- Anthony Albanese has been a member of the Australian House of Representatives since 1996.\n- Anthony Albanese represents the Division of Grayndler for the Australian Labor Party and serves as the party's spokesperson on Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism.\n- On 27 June 2013, Governor-General Quentin Bryce swore in three members of the Second Rudd Ministry.\n- The three sworn-in members were Kevin Rudd as Prime Minister, Anthony Albanese as Deputy Prime Minister, and Chris Bowen as Treasurer.\n- The Second Rudd Ministry was the 68th ministry of the Australian government and was led by Prime Minister Kevin Rudd.",
